# CMake Conventions

## Source lists
Never use `file(GLOB ...)` — list source files explicitly so additions are visible in diffs.

```cmake
# ❌ BAD
file(GLOB SOURCES "*.cpp")

# ✅ GOOD
add_library(telemetry
    Framer.cpp
    Parser.cpp
    ParserWorker.cpp
)
```

## Library types
Follow the existing pattern in `src/CMakeLists.txt`:
- `INTERFACE` — header-only aggregates (e.g. `cosmo-backend`)
- `STATIC` — self-contained, no Qt dependency (e.g. `import`)
- `OBJECT` — lightweight internal modules (e.g. `flight`, `persistence`)

## Dependencies
- Every new `find_package` or `target_link_libraries` entry must have an inline comment explaining why it is needed
- Do not add new third-party libraries without updating this file and `README.md`

## Platform guards
Wrap platform-specific subdirectories with `if(UNIX)` / `if(WIN32)` — never assume a platform silently.
